  <para style="h">Ñwed Mbon Efisọs</para>
  <para style="toc1">Ñwed Mbon Efisọs</para>
  <para style="toc2">Ñwed Mbon Efisọs</para>
  <para style="toc3">Efi</para>
  <para style="mt1">Ñwed Mbon Efisọs</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="EPH 1" />
  <para style="s1">Ekọọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 1:1" />Ami Pọọl, abọsịd Krais Yisọs ke uduak Abasi, nnọ ñwed ami esọk mme ndisana ikọd Abasi ke Efisọs, mme andisọọñọ nda ke Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="EPH 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 1:2" />Yak mfọn ye emem a-atooho Abasi Ete Ñnyịn ye Abọọñ Yisọs Krais aba ye ndufo.<verse eid="EPH 1:2" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekọọm a-Abañake Mme Enọ Sịbidịd ke Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 1:3" />Itooro anie Abasi ye Ete Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais, a-amaakidiọñ ñnyịn ke ebekpo ubọọñ ye afịd adidiọñ Sịbidịd ke Krais. <verse eid="EPH 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 1:4" />Sia anye ke idem amọ amaimek ñnyịn ke Krais mbemiso ekebot ederimbod ate isana inyʌñ inana ndo ke iso amọ. Ke ima <verse eid="EPH 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 1:5" />anye amaimek ñnyịn ke adiben ñnyịn mbon nte nditọ ato Yisọs Krais, nte asañake akekem ke inemesịd ye uduak amọ, <verse eid="EPH 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 1:6" />ke itooro ye ubọọñ mfọn amọ, a-anye inọọhọ ñnyịn ke mfọn ato Krais a-anye amaaha. <verse eid="EPH 1:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 1:7" />Ke anye ke ñnyịn inie ufak ato iyiib amọ, adifeen mme idiọọkñkpọ, a-asañake akekem ye mme inie e-etooho mfọn Abasi <verse eid="EPH 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 1:8" />a-anye akenwaññake ifʌk ñnyịn. Ye afịd aniọñ ye adinam anwaña, <verse eid="EPH 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 1:9" />anye amaanam ñnyịn idiọọñọ ndedịbe uduak amọ naña asaña akekem ke inemesịd amọ, a-anye amaakeduaduak ke Krais, <verse eid="EPH 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 1:10" />a-adiinam awuọ ada ayọhọ-ayọhọ ke ini amaadikem, nọ eben afịd ñkpọ ke abio Abasi ye ke isọñ edian keed ke idak ukara Krais.<verse eid="EPH 1:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 1:11" />Ke anye, emaenyʌñ imek ñnyịn i-imaikibaba tọọñọ ke aditọọñọ, nte asañake akekem ke ubonoñkpọ anye a-anamma afịd ñkpọ asio nọ asaña ye ewʌhọ uduak amọ, <verse eid="EPH 1:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 1:12" />nọ ato do, ñnyịn i-ikidooho akpa adidot anyen ke Krais, ikan ikwọ itooro mfọn amọ. <verse eid="EPH 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 1:13" />Ndin emaenyʌñ isịn ndufo ke Krais ke imaikikop ikọ akpanikọ, adooho eti etob adinyaaña ndufo. Ke imaikinịm ke akpanikọ, emainịm ndufo idiọọñọ ke ufiikñkpọ Adisana Sịbidịd e-ekenwọñọke, <verse eid="EPH 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 1:14" />a-adooho ubiọñ udeeme akpa ñnyịn tutu ini adinyaaña mbon e-edoññoke ake Abasi, ke itooro ubọọñ amọ.<verse eid="EPH 1:14" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekọọm ye Akam</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 1:15" />Ke ntak ami, tọọñọ ami ñkekop mbaña mbuọdidem ndufo ke Abọọñ Yisọs dian ima a-ndufo enieghe enọọ afịd ndisana nditọ Abasi, <verse eid="EPH 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 1:16" />ami ntreke adinọ ekọọm ibaña ndufo, ke adikaiso itoiyo ndufo ke akam. <verse eid="EPH 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 1:17" />Ami nsʌk ñkakaiso mbeeñe mbo yak Abasi Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais, Ete andibọ ubọọñ, inọ ndufo Sịbidịd aniọñ ye adiyaara, nọ ndufo ediọọñọ anye afọn akan ami. <verse eid="EPH 1:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 1:18" />Ami mmenyʌñ mbọñ akam mbo yak enam anyen esịd ndufo anwaña nọ ato do ndufo ediọọñọ idodanyen a-anye ikoodo ndufo, ye inie ubọọñ afịd ndisana ikọd amọ, <verse eid="EPH 1:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 1:19" />ye ananambid akpọsọñ adudu i-inọọhọ ñnyịn mme andinịm ke akpanikọ. Adudu ado ado ukem akpọsọñ adudu amọ, <verse eid="EPH 1:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 1:20" />a-anye akekamake anam Krais aset ke ñkpa anyʌñ atem anye ke ubọk nnasia amọ ke mme ikpeghe ebekpo hefịn, <verse eid="EPH 1:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 1:21" />a-akoñño akan afịd ukara ye adudu ye afịd ubọọñ, ye afịd anyịñ se ekpekakan adikoot, idooho ke emana ami ikpọọñ ado ye ke emana adiidi. <verse eid="EPH 1:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EPH 1:22" />Ndin Abasi amaasịn afịd ñkpọ ke idak ukod amọ anyʌñ amek anye adido adaiwuod nnọọ afịd ñkpọ ke ufọkabasi, <verse eid="EPH 1:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EPH 1:23" />a-adooho idem amọ, uyọhọ anye a-anamma afịd ñkpọ ayọhọ ke afịd usʌñ.<verse eid="EPH 1:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="EPH 2" />
  <para style="s1">Adimaana Ndu Uwem ke Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 2:1" />Amaado ndufo, emaekpañña ke ntak ndiọiñkpọ ye ndudue ndufo, <verse eid="EPH 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 2:2" />a-ndufo ekenamma ke adikikeene ndʌk mme usʌñ ederimbod ami, ye adikeene andida ukara ubọọñ ke ikpeghe afịm, sịbidịd a-anamma utom idahami ke idem mbon ntreutọñ. <verse eid="EPH 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 2:3" />Ini keed ko, afịd ñnyịn ikinyʌñ iba ke atu ammọ, inyʌñ idu uwem inọ adiyʌkkọ iwʌd abʌkidem ye adikeene mme udọñ ye mme akikere amọ. Kpa nte mbon mfen, tọọñọ ke emana ñnyịn ikidoñño ñkpọ iyadesịd Abasi. <verse eid="EPH 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 2:4" />Ado ke ntak ekamba ima a-anye anieghe inọọ ñnyịn, Abasi a-mbọm amọ akponno, <verse eid="EPH 2:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 2:5" />amaanam ñnyịn idu uwem ye Krais akpesʌkado ñnyịn imaikikpañña ke mme ukwañ ñkpọ, ado ato ke mfọn ke ndufo ebọọ adinyaaña. <verse eid="EPH 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 2:6" />Ndin Abasi amaanam ñnyịn iset ye Krais anyʌñ anam ñnyịn itie ye anye ke mme ikpeghe abioubọọñ hefịn ke Krais Yisọs, <verse eid="EPH 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 2:7" />nọ ato do ke mme isua a-adiidi, anye adiikan iwọt ananambid uwak mfọn amọ a-anye anamma nọ ikem ñnyịn ke mfọnido amọ ye ñnyịn ke Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="EPH 2:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 2:8" />Sia ke mfọn ke inyaaña ndufo, ato mbuọdidem, ndin anye ami itooho ndufo, ado ado enọ a-atooho Abasi, <verse eid="EPH 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 2:9" />idooho ke mme utom, mbaak awo ndomokeed adiduaak inua. <verse eid="EPH 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 2:10" />Sia ñnyịn ido ubọkutom Abasi e-ekebotto ke Krais Yisọs ete inam nti utom, A-Abasi amaakebebem iso abeeñe anịm inọọ ñnyịn adinam.<verse eid="EPH 2:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Emem ke Ufọọd mme Yuu ye mme Gentile</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 2:11" />Ke ntoro, itoiyo ke ndufo e-ekedooho mme Gentile ke emana a-mbon “e-efọọrọke edʌd” ikootto ndufo “mbon i-imiifọọroke edʌd” (e-ekamake ubọk awo enam ke ikpọkidem) <verse eid="EPH 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 2:12" />itoiyo ke ndufo emaediañña ekpọñ Krais, ikisịneke ke atu nditọ Isrel, ekenyʌñ edoñño isen ke abaña akaaña enwọñọ, enana idodanyen enyʌñ enana Abasi ke ederimbod. <verse eid="EPH 2:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 2:13" />Ado idahami, ke Krais Yisọs, e-enam ndufo e-ekedaaha nsan-nsan esaña ekpere ke iyiib Krais.<verse eid="EPH 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 2:14" />Sia anye ke idem amọ ado emem ñnyịn, a-amaakenam mme Yuu ye mme Gentile ekappa edo keed ndin amaanyʌñ abiat ñkpọ ubiọọñọ ye ndibene ubakka ye ndusuara <verse eid="EPH 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 2:15" />ke adiben mbed ye mme ewʌhọ ye ndutʌm unañña ñkpọ mfep ke ikpọkidem amọ. Uduak amọ akedo adibot ke idem amọ ufa uduud awo keed, ñnyʌñ nsịn emem ke adinam ntoro. <verse eid="EPH 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 2:16" />Ndin ke abʌkidem keed anye asịn emem ke ufọọd ammọ ye Abasi ato ke krọs a-anye adatta awot ndusuara ammọ. <verse eid="EPH 2:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 2:17" />Anye amaadi adikwọrọ emem inọ ndufo e-ekebaaha ke anyan usʌñ anyʌñ akwọrọ emem anọ mbon e-ekebaaha ekpere. <verse eid="EPH 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 2:18" />Sia ke anye afịd ñnyịn iminie ufañ adisaña ñkpere Abasi ke Sịbidịd keed.<verse eid="EPH 2:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 2:19" />Ke ntoro ndufo idooho aba mme adidʌñ ye mme isenawo, ado ekeene edo mme amanaisọñ ye ikọd Abasi ye mbon esịd ufọk amọ, <verse eid="EPH 2:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 2:20" />e-enịmme mme abọsịd ye mme prọfed nte itiad idakisọñ ye Krais Yisọs ke idem amọ nte etubom itiad inuuk. <verse eid="EPH 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 2:21" />Ato ke anye afịd ufọk adiana keed anyʌñ akappa adisana tembịd ke Abọọñ. <verse eid="EPH 2:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EPH 2:22" />Ndin ke anye i-ibọp ndufo edian keed nọ ekappa itie idʌñ A-Abasi adʌññọ ke Sịbidịd amọ.<verse eid="EPH 2:22" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="EPH 3" />
  <para style="s1">Utịppe Uduak A-Abasi Anieghe Anọ mme Gentile</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 3:1" />Ke ntak ami ke ami Pọọl ndo awo ñkpakọb Krais Yisọs ke ntak ndufo mme Gentile.<verse eid="EPH 3:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 3:2" />Mmenịm ke ndufo emekop ebaña mfọn A-Abasi akennọọhọ miin ke ntak ndufo, <verse eid="EPH 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 3:3" />a-adooho ndedịbe ñkpọ e-ekenamma ndiọọñọ ke adiyaara, nte mmaakewewet ibio-ibio. <verse eid="EPH 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 3:4" />Ndufo imaikoot ñwed ami, ayaanekke inwaña ndufo ifiọk a-ami nnieghe mbaña ndedịbe ñkpọ Krais, <verse eid="EPH 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 3:5" />e-ediikiyaarake inọ mme awo ke mme emana mfen naña Sịbidịd Abasi ayaara idahami ke mme ndisana abọsịd ye mme prọfed. <verse eid="EPH 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 3:6" />Ndedịbe ñkpọ ado ado ke ntak eti etob mme Gentile edoñño mme adiaakpa ubon Isrel, e-ebatta edian keed ubon Abasi, e-enyʌññọ ewuana keed ke enwọñọ ke Krais Yisọs.<verse eid="EPH 3:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 3:7" />Ato ke mfọn A-Abasi annọọhọ miin ami mmaakappa ndo afʌn ikọabasi, ato utom adudu amọ. <verse eid="EPH 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 3:8" />Akpesʌkado a-ami nsuuhọke itie ñkan andisịp ñkan ke atu ikọd Abasi, ekennọ miin mfọn ami adikwọrọ nnọọ mme Gentile mme inie ke Krais a-awo imiikanna idiọọñọ, <verse eid="EPH 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 3:9" />adinyʌñ nnam ndedịbe enọ ami anwaña afịd awo, a-adooho ke mme ayio a-akeboiyoke ekedeedịp ke Abasi a-akebotto afịd ñkpọ. <verse eid="EPH 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 3:10" />Udọñ amọ akedo yak ato ke ufọkabasi, mme ukara ye mme adudu ke mme ikpeghe ebekpo ubọọñ ediọọñọ ebaña akwa ananambid aniọñ Abasi, <verse eid="EPH 3:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 3:11" />nọ asaña akekem ke nsi-nsi uduak amọ a-anye akenamma asu ke Krais Yisọs Abọọñ ñnyịn. <verse eid="EPH 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 3:12" />Ke anye, ato ñko ke mbuọdidem ke anye, ñnyịn imikan adisaña ñkpere Abasi ke ñkpọkñyak ye uko. <verse eid="EPH 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 3:13" />Ke ntoro, ami idọkkọ ndufo mbo ikiiyak idem imem ndufo ke ntak ukuud a-ami mbọọhọ ke ntak ndufo, a-adooho ubọọñ ndufo.<verse eid="EPH 3:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ebọñ Akam Enọ Mbon Efisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 3:14" />Ke ntak ami, mmetọọñọ edọñ ke iso Abasi, <verse eid="EPH 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 3:15" />a-afịd ubon ke abio Abasi ye ke ederimbod enieghe anyịñ eto. <verse eid="EPH 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 3:16" />Ami mbọñ akam mbo ke ntak mfọn ye ubọọñ amọ, anye inọ ndufo nsọọñọnda ye adudu a-atooho Sịbidịd amọ ke esịd ndufo, <verse eid="EPH 3:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 3:17" />nọ Krais adʌñ ke esịd ndufo ato ke mbuọdidem. Ñnyʌñ mbọñ akam ñko nte ndufo i-imaikisọọñọ ida ke ima, <verse eid="EPH 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 3:18" />ekan enie adudu, ediana ye afịd ndisana nditọ Abasi, nọ se ido ubom ye unyọọñ ye anyan ye ntəño ima Krais atʌm inwaña ndufo, <verse eid="EPH 3:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 3:19" />ñko nọ ediọọñọ ima a-akanna ifiọk nọ ndufo ekan eyọhọ ke udomo afịd uyọhọ Abasi.<verse eid="EPH 3:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 3:20" />Ndin yak anye a-akanna anam akan se ebeñe me se ekere, nte asañake akekem ke adudu a-anamma utom ke idem ñnyịn, <verse eid="EPH 3:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 3:21" />abọ ubọọñ ke ufọkabasi ye ke Krais Yisọs ke afịd mme emana, ke nsi-nsi nsi-nsi! Amen.<verse eid="EPH 3:21" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="EPH 4" />
  <para style="s1">Adidiana Keed ye Ndiọọñọidem ke Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 4:1" />Nte awo ñkpakọb Abọọñ, ami mmikpeiye ndufo nte edu uwem a-adotto ikood a-ndufo ebọọhọ. <verse eid="EPH 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 4:2" />Isuuhọ idem ataa afịd-afịd, inyʌñ iba emem-emem; inie ime, iyọ emọ-emọ ke ima. <verse eid="EPH 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 4:3" />Idomo afịd ukeme adidiana keed ke Sịbidịd ato ke emem i-idianna ndufo keed. <verse eid="EPH 4:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 4:4" />Idem keed aba, Sịbidịd keed anyʌñ aba, kpa naña ekikoot ndufo ke idodanyen keed ke ini ekikoodo ndufo; <verse eid="EPH 4:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 4:5" />Abọọñ keed, mbuọdidem keed, uduọkmmọọñ keed; <verse eid="EPH 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 4:6" />Abasi keed ye Ete afịd awo, a-akarake afịd ñkpọ, ato afịd awo anyʌñ asịne ke idem afịd awo.<verse eid="EPH 4:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 4:7" />Ado, i-inọ ñnyịn keedekeed mfọn akeene naña Krais adeeme. <verse eid="EPH 4:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 4:8" />Ntak ado anam ikọ Abasi abo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EPH 4:8">“Ke anye amaakedọọk ke anyọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EPH 4:8">anye amaadat uwak awo nte mbon ñkpakọb</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EPH 4:8">anyʌñ adeeme mme enọ anọ ikọd amọ.”<verse eid="EPH 4:8" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 4:9" />(Nsoo ke “anye amaakedọọk” awuọñọ, ke imiibọhọke ke anye amaasọiyọ adʌk usuuhọ mme ikpeghe isọñ? <verse eid="EPH 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 4:10" />Anye a-akesọiyọke anyʌñ ado anye a-akedọọhọ akoñ akan afịd mme hefịn, nọ anye ayọhọ afịd ekondo.) <verse eid="EPH 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 4:11" />Ke ntoro Krais ke idem amọ akenọọ mme abọsịd, mme prọfed, mme ifanyere, usʌk mme akwọrọikọ ye mme andikpeeb, <verse eid="EPH 4:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 4:12" />adibeeñe ikọd amọ idem nnịm nnọ utom unọ unwam, nọ ekan ebọp adisana idem Krais, a-adooho ufọkabasi <verse eid="EPH 4:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 4:13" />tutu afịd ñnyịn inie adidiana keed ke mbuọdidem ye ifiọk ke Ayịn Abasi inyʌñ inie ndiọọñọidem isịm afịd uyọhọ Krais.<verse eid="EPH 4:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 4:14" />Ndin ñnyịn idiidooho nsek nditọ a-afịm anəkko aka iso ye edem, ndin afịm ukpeeb ye afịd ñkara ye ndukanna mme awo ke nsu ammọ iben ñnyịn atọ ke nnasia ye ufiin. <verse eid="EPH 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 4:15" />Utu ke ado, ke aditañ akpanikọ ke ima, ke afịd usʌñ ñnyịn iyaikọt inyʌñ ikpoon idʌk ke idem anye a-adooho iwuod, a-adooho Krais. <verse eid="EPH 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 4:16" />Ato ke anye afịd idem, e-emaekekama nsio-nsio asịb ibọp edian keed, akọt anyʌñ abọp idem amọ adian ke ima, naña ñkek keedekeed enam utom ammọ.<verse eid="EPH 4:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Item Adidu Uwem Nte Ikọd Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 4:17" />Ke ntoro, ami idọkkọ ndufo, ñnyʌñ mmaana nsọọñọ mbo ke idak Abọọñ, ke inaaha ndufo ekaiso edu uwem aba nte mme Gentile enamma ato ke uyaha akikere ammọ. <verse eid="EPH 4:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 4:18" />Ifiọk ammọ ado ñkịm-ñkịm, anyʌñ asịkke ammọ akpọñ uwem Abasi ato ke unana adidiọọñọ a-asịneke ammọ ke idem ato ntak isọñesịd ammọ. <verse eid="EPH 4:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 4:19" />Sia ammọ enanake iso abuud, ammọ eyaak idem ammọ enyiin ke mme nsio-nsio ndiọi udọñ abʌkidem a-anamma nọ ammọ ekaiso ke afịd ndedeghe eduuwem, enyʌñ eyọhọ ye udọrọ itọñ.<verse eid="EPH 4:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 4:20" />Ado idooho utọ eduuwem ami ke ndufo ekekpeep ke ini ndufo ekekoppo ebaña Krais, <verse eid="EPH 4:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 4:21" />e-ekenyʌññọ ikpeep ndufo ke anye nte asañake akekem ke akpanikọ a-asịneke ke Yisọs. <verse eid="EPH 4:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EPH 4:22" />Ke abaña ñkaan eduuwem ndufo, emaikpeep ndufo ete eduọñọ ñkaan eduuwem ndufo amaakebiaña ato ke mme abiaña-abiaña udọñ, <verse eid="EPH 4:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EPH 4:23" />nọ enam ndufo edo ufa ke akikere ndufo; <verse eid="EPH 4:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EPH 4:24" />enyʌñ eben ufa idem esịne, e-ekebotto nọ aba nte Abasi ke nnen-nnen ido ye adisana uwem.<verse eid="EPH 4:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EPH 4:25" />Ke ntoro ana afịd ndufo etre nsu enyʌñ etañ akpanikọ enọ keed ye aken, sia afịd ñnyịn idoñño ñkek idem keed. <verse eid="EPH 4:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EPH 4:26" />“Ikiinam iyadesịd inam ndufo enam idiọọkñkpọ.” Ikiiyak utịn asuuhọ adisịme ndufo naña esʌk eyayat esịd, <verse eid="EPH 4:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EPH 4:27" />ñko ikiinyʌñ inọọ andidiọọk ndomo mbeñe ufañ adiboiyo ndʌk. <verse eid="EPH 4:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EPH 4:28" />Awo ndomokeed a-asiyịppe inọ inaaha ayịp aba, ado ana anam utom, anam ñkpọ se ifọn ke ubọk amọ, nọ anye anie ñkpọ se akan adiañña anọ mbon unana.<verse eid="EPH 4:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="EPH 4:29" />Ikiiyak idiọọk ikọ ndomokeed iwuọ ndufo ke inua, ado yak ado se ikan inwam adisọọñọ mme awo idem ke unana ammọ, nọ mbon e-ekpañña utọñ ebọ ufọn ñko. <verse eid="EPH 4:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EPH 4:30" />Ikiinyʌñ inọọ Adisana Sịbidịd Abasi mbʌññọ esịd, anye e-ekebenne ifiik ndufo idiọọñọ tutu usen adifak. <verse eid="EPH 4:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EPH 4:31" />Itoomo afịd idiọọkesịd, abom ye iyadesịd, anwan ye ikọ, adidọk ye afịd udod awo uyio iduọọñọ. <verse eid="EPH 4:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EPH 4:32" />Ifọn ido inyʌñ ikop mbọm ibaña emọ-emọ, ifeen inọ emọ-emọ kpa naña Abasi akefeen inọọ ndufo ke Krais.<verse eid="EPH 4:32" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="EPH 5" />
  <para style="s1">Adidu Uwem Ñkeene Uwọdñkpọ Krais</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 5:1" />Ke ntoro, ikeene uwọdñkpọ Abasi, sia edoññoke nditọ a-anye anekkeke ama, <verse eid="EPH 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 5:2" />inyʌñ inie ima, kpa naña Krais akima ñnyịn, a-akenyʌññọ ayaak uwem amọ anọ Abasi ke ntak ñnyịn nte anemufịk enọ ye uwa.<verse eid="EPH 5:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 5:3" />Ado inaaha ñkpọ ndomokeed a-abañake use aba ke atu ndufo, me ndedeghe uwem ndomokeed, me idiọọkitọñ, sia mme ñkpọ ami ifọnnọ ke atu ndisana ikọd Abasi. <verse eid="EPH 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 5:4" />Ñko atịme-atịme uwem inaaha aba, ye ndisịme ikọ me ñyọọ i-imiidotto, ado yak enọ ekọọm ikpọọñ. <verse eid="EPH 5:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 5:5" />Sia ana ndufo enekke ediọọñọ ami: Ibaaha anam use me asịn efịbe, ndedeghe awo me awo idiọọkitọñ, (utọ awo ntoro ado akpono ndem), a-anieghe udeeme ndomokeed ke abioubọọñ Krais<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5:5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akeme isʌk ndo </char><char style="fq" closed="false">abioubọọñ </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">aka Mesaiya ye ake Abasi</char></note>, ye ake Abasi. <verse eid="EPH 5:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 5:6" />Yak awo ndomokeed akuuyaañ fiin ke uyaha ikọ sia ato ke ntak ñkpọ ntoro iyadesịd Abasi adoro mbon ntreutọñ. <verse eid="EPH 5:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 5:7" />Ke ntoro, ikiidʌk nsaña ye ammọ.<verse eid="EPH 5:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 5:8" />Sia ini keed ko ndufo ekedo ekịm, ado idahami, ndufo edo unwana ke Abọọñ. Idu uwem nte nditọ unwana <verse eid="EPH 5:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 5:9" />(sia mfịd unwana asịne ke afịd mfọnido, adinenido ye akpanikọ) <verse eid="EPH 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 5:10" />inyʌñ idiọọñọ ñkpọ se inem Abọọñ esịd. <verse eid="EPH 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 5:11" />Ikiinie ewuana ndomokeed ye mme utom ekịm imiibaaha ufọn, utu ke ado iyaara ammọ. <verse eid="EPH 5:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 5:12" />Sia ado ataa ñkpọ abuud idem aditatañ se mbon ntreutọñ esinam ke ndịbe. <verse eid="EPH 5:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 5:13" />Ado e-ekịt afịd ñkpọ se unwana ayaara, ndin afịd ñkpọ se unwana atuuk akappa ado unwana. <verse eid="EPH 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 5:14" />Ntak ebooho ntom ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="EPH 5:14">“Demme, afo adaiya idab,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EPH 5:14">set ke ñkpa,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="EPH 5:14">ndin Krais ayaayamma unọ fiin.”<verse eid="EPH 5:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 5:15" />Ndin inekke ikpeme naña ndufo edu uwem, ke ado nte mme anana aniọñ, ado nte mbon aniọñ, <verse eid="EPH 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 5:16" />itʌm idat ufañ e-enieghe inam eti ñkpọ, sia mme usen ifọnnọ. <verse eid="EPH 5:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 5:17" />Ke ntoro, ikiidoñño ndisịme, ado yak uduak Abọọñ inwaña ndufo. <verse eid="EPH 5:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 5:18" />Ikiikpa mmịn, a-asañake ye adisappa idem. Utu ke ado, iyọhọ ye Sịbidịd. <verse eid="EPH 5:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 5:19" />Ikama mme saam, mme ikwọ, ye mme ikwọ etooho Sịbidịd ineme nneme ye emọ-emọ. Ikwọ inyʌñ ibre ikwọ a-atooho esịd ndufo inọ Abọọñ. <verse eid="EPH 5:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 5:20" />Afịd-afịd ini, inọ Abasi andido Ete ekọọm ke abaña afịd ñkpọ ke anyịñ Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais.<verse eid="EPH 5:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Item A-anieghe Ubon Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 5:21" />Isuuho iwuod inọ emọ-emọ ke ntak Krais.<verse eid="EPH 5:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="EPH 5:22" />Ibaan ndọ isuuho idem inọ mme ebe ndufo, nte esuuhọ enọ Abọọñ. <verse eid="EPH 5:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EPH 5:23" />Sia ebe ado iwuod anọ anwaan nte Krais adooho iwuod anọ ufọkabasi, a-adooho idem amọ, a-anye anyʌññọ ado Andinyaaña. <verse eid="EPH 5:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EPH 5:24" />Ndin, naña ufọkabasi asuuhọ iwuod anọ Krais, akpena ibaan esuuk iwuod enọ mme ebe ammọ ke afịd ñkpọ.<verse eid="EPH 5:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="EPH 5:25" />Mme ebe, ima ibaan ndufo, kpa naña Krais akema ufọkabasi anyʌñ asaana idem amọ ayaak anọ anye, <verse eid="EPH 5:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EPH 5:26" />nọ anam anye ado adisana, asịññe anye mbad ke adiyet ke mmọọñ ato ke ikọ, <verse eid="EPH 5:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EPH 5:27" />nọ anyʌñ aben anye ayaak anọ idem amọ nte ufọkabasi a-ayammake ke ubọọñ, inieghe mbad me ñkịd, ibiomoke ndo ndomokeed, ndin ado adisana, anyʌñ anana ndo. <verse eid="EPH 5:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EPH 5:28" />Ke ukem usʌñ ami, ana mme ebe ema ibaan ammọ. Awo a-amaaha anwaan amọ ama idem amọ. <verse eid="EPH 5:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EPH 5:29" />Ke adinekke nse, kpaanam awo ndomokeed isuaha idem amọ, ado anọ anye ndidia anyʌñ akama anye afọn, kpa naña Krais ama ufọkabasi. <verse eid="EPH 5:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EPH 5:30" />Sia ñnyịn ido mme ndido idem amọ. <verse eid="EPH 5:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EPH 5:31" />“Ke ntak ami, awodeen ayaakpọñ ete ye eka amọ akediana ye anwaan amọ, ndin ammọ awo iba eyaekappa edo abʌk keed.” <verse eid="EPH 5:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EPH 5:32" />Ami ado ataa ntọtʌñọ ñkpọ a-ayaññake awo ifiọk, ado ami ntañ mbaña Krais ye ufọkabasi. <verse eid="EPH 5:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EPH 5:33" />Kpayeado, awo keedekeed ana ama anwaan amọ naña anye ama idem amọ, ndin ana anwaan akpono ebe amọ.<verse eid="EPH 5:33" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="EPH 6" />
  <para style="s1">Nditọ ye mme Unie Ammọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="EPH 6:1" />Nditọ, ikop item inọ mme ete ye mme eka ndufo ke Abọọñ, sia a-anen adinam ntoro. <verse eid="EPH 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EPH 6:2" />“Kpono ete ye eka mfo,” ado akpa mbed a-asañake ye enwọñọ, <verse eid="EPH 6:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EPH 6:3" />“nọ afọn ye afo, nọ afo anyʌñ adu anyan uwem ke isọñ.”<verse eid="EPH 6:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="EPH 6:4" />Mme ete, ikiinam nditọ ndufo eyat esịd, ado ikama ammọ ke ukpeeb ye item ke Abọọñ.<verse eid="EPH 6:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="EPH 6:5" />Mme ifʌn, ikop item inyʌñ ibaak mme eteufọk ndufo ke ederimbod ke esịd akpanikọ, kpa naña ekpekop item enọọ Krais. <verse eid="EPH 6:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EPH 6:6" />Isuuk iwuod inọ ammọ, idooho ke adibọ itooro utom anyen awo ikpọọñ ke iso ammọ, ado nte ekpedooho ifʌn Krais, enam uduak Abasi ke awọñesịd ndufo. <verse eid="EPH 6:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EPH 6:7" />Inam ke afịd esịd, nte enam enọ Abọọñ idooho awo, <verse eid="EPH 6:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EPH 6:8" />sia ndufo emediọọñọ ke Abọọñ ayaanọ afịd awo utịb ke afịd nti ñkpọ a-ammọ enamma, adooho anye ado afʌn me amanaisọñ.<verse eid="EPH 6:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="EPH 6:9" />Ndin mme eteufọk, ikama mme ifʌn ndufo ke ukem usʌñ ado. Ikiisịn ammọ ndịk ke idem, sia ndufo emediọọñọ ke anye a-adooho Ete anọ ammọ ye ndufo aba ke hefịn, ndin adusad ibaaha ke anye.<verse eid="EPH 6:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Ñkpọekọñ Abasi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="EPH 6:10" />Ke akpatre, isọọñọ ida ke Abọọñ ye ke akpọsọñ adudu amọ. <verse eid="EPH 6:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EPH 6:11" />Isịne afịd ñkpọekọñ Abasi nọ ekan eda ke idaha adinwana afịd ñkara andidiọọk. <verse eid="EPH 6:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EPH 6:12" />Sia anwan ñnyịn idooho ye abʌk ye iyiib, ado ye mme andikara, ye mme adudu, ye mme adudu ekịm ederimbod ami, ye mme ndiọi adudu a-sịbidịd ke mme ikpeghe ebekpo anyọñ. <verse eid="EPH 6:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EPH 6:13" />Ke ntoro, iben afịd ñkpọekọñ Abasi isịne ke idem, nọ ato do mme idiọọk usen amaadi, ndufo ediikan isọọñọ ida ke iwuuk ndufo, ndin ndufo imainam afịd ñkpọ ima, isọọñọ ida. <verse eid="EPH 6:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EPH 6:14" />Isọọñọ ida ndin, ikịne ñkpaha akpanikọ ke isịn, ye ukwak ikpanesịd adinenido ke itie amọ, <verse eid="EPH 6:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EPH 6:15" />ndin inam ukod ndufo aba ke mbeeñeidem a-atooho eti mbʌk emem. <verse eid="EPH 6:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EPH 6:16" />Ke edianna afịd ami, iben ñkpọekọñ mbuọdidem ikama, a-ndufo ekanna adidat nniime akpọsọñ idañ ikañ andidiọọk. <verse eid="EPH 6:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EPH 6:17" />Ibenne itam adinyaaña iyara, ye akañkañ Sịbidịd, a-adooho ikọ Abasi.<verse eid="EPH 6:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="EPH 6:18" />Inyʌñ idat mme nsio-nsio ukod akam ye mme ebeeñe ibọñ akam ke Sịbidịd afịd ini. Ye akikere ami ke esịd, itịñ anyen inyʌñ ibọñ akam afịd ini inọ afịd mme ndisana ikọd Abasi. <verse eid="EPH 6:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EPH 6:19" />Ibọñ akam innọ miin ñko, ite ini akeedodo a-ami ñkʌppọke inua, yak ennọ miin ikọ nọ ntañ uko-uko, nọ nnam ediọọñọ mme ndedịbe ñkpọ eti etob <verse eid="EPH 6:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EPH 6:20" />a-ami ndooho isʌñutom nnọ ke ñkpakọb. Ibọñ akam nọ ami ñkan ñkwọrọ anye uko-uko naña akpenaa nte nnam.<verse eid="EPH 6:20" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="s1">Akpatre Ekọọm</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="EPH 6:21" />Tikikọs, adima ayịneka awodeen ye ataa eti anam akpanikọ isʌñutom ke Abọọñ, ayaidọkkọ ndufo afịd ñkpọ, nọ ndufo ñko ediọọñọ naña aba ye ami ye se ami nnam. <verse eid="EPH 6:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EPH 6:22" />Ami ndọñ anye inọ ndufo ke ntak ami, nọ ndufo ediọọñọ naña aba ye ñnyịn, nọ anye anyʌñ isọọñọ ndufo idem.<verse eid="EPH 6:22" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="EPH 6:23" />Yak emem aba ye nditọeka<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6:23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek adelfọi a-adaaha anọ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nditọeka </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ideen ye ibaan</char><char style="ft" closed="false">anyʌñ asʌk ada anọ ideen ye ibaan e-enịmme Krais ke akpanikọ, ke atu ubon Abasi.</char></note> ke Krais, ye ima a-asañake ye mbuọdidem ato Abasi Ete ye Abọọñ Yisọs Krais.<verse eid="EPH 6:23" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="EPH 6:24" />Yak mfọn aba ye afịd awo e-emaaha Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais ye nsi-nsi ima.<verse eid="EPH 6:24" /></para>
  <chapter eid="EPH 6" />
</usx>